e and Mr.&#160;Ernst provides the Company with a release of claims, Mr.&#160;Ernst shall be entitled to receive a cash severance payment in the amount of one hundred&#160;percent (100%) of his then current base salary and one&#160;year of COBRA continuation coverage.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Thomas I. Brown</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt;">In the event Mr. Brown&#8217;s employment agreement is terminated by the Company without cause or by Mr. Brown for good reason, and Mr. Brown provides the Company with a release of claims, Mr. Brown would be entitled to receive a severance payment equal to one hundred percent (100%) of his then-current base salary, payable over a twelve-month period, as well </p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">13</p></div></div>
